exports[`generateBridges > target gemini snapshot 1`] = `
"# GEMINI.md — Hivelore context

<!-- haive:bridge-start -->
<!-- AUTO-GENERATED by hivelore bridges sync — do not edit between these markers -->

<!-- Managed by Hivelore. Edit OUTSIDE the hivelore markers only; the marked blocks are regenerated. -->

This repo uses **[Hivelore](https://github.com/Doucs91/hivelore)** for shared, enforced team context.
The corpus lives in \`.ai/\` and is the source of truth — these files are only a small breadcrumb map.
Keep default context small; pull deeper memories, code maps, or docs only when the task needs them.

- \`.ai/project-context.md\` — project overview, architecture, conventions.
- \`.ai/memories/\` — decisions, gotchas, conventions, failed attempts (personal/team/module).
- The blocks below are top breadcrumbs + the hard rules enforced on commit.

## Working through Hivelore

Hooks deliver the rules for each file you edit, and the commit gate checks the diff — there is no ritual.
Reach for Hivelore when it helps you:

1. **Unfamiliar code**: \`why <file>:<line>\` (MCP or \`hivelore why\`) — the rules, sensors, doc warnings and past
   fixes for that line. Starting a substantive task in an area you do not know: \`get_briefing\` with task + files.
2. **A lesson worth keeping**: an approach that failed for a real reason → \`mem_tried\` (what, why, instead).
   The developer states a lasting rule → offer once to record it (\`mem_save\`, one-line \`rule\`) and to arm it
   (\`propose_sensor\`). A verified decision says how (\`verified_by\`) and what that could not see (\`cannot_detect\`).
   No session recaps: commits and the PR say what was done.
3. **CI is red**: \`hivelore ci why\`. **Before reporting done**: \`hivelore enforce finish\` — it judges only the
   files this task changed; never commit, ignore or delete files that were modified before the task started.

If MCP is unavailable, use \`hivelore briefing --files <paths> --task <task>\`, or read \`.ai/project-context.md\` and search \`.ai/memories/\`. Report the unavailable integration.

## Safety

- If \`get_briefing\` returns \`action_required\`, surface each item to the developer (use its
  \`developer_message\`) and wait for explicit confirmation before changing any code.
- Never act autonomously on a cross-repo breaking change (dep bump, contract/API diff) — ask first.

## Memories

<!-- haive:memories-start -->
<!-- AUTO-GENERATED by hivelore bridges sync — do not edit between these markers -->
<!-- Top breadcrumbs only — call get_briefing / mem_get for deeper context. -->

- \`2026-01-01-decision-use-validated\` (team/decision) — Always prefer newApi() over oldApi().

<!-- haive:memories-end -->

<!-- haive:sensors-start -->
<!-- AUTO-GENERATED by hivelore bridges sync — do not edit between these markers -->

## Hard rules — Hivelore block sensors

The patterns below are blocked by the repo enforcement gate.
Introducing them will fail the pre-commit check (\`hivelore enforce check\`).

Wrong about one specific line? Waive that line — \`// hivelore:allow <memory-id> — <reason>\` at
end of line — instead of deleting the rule or rewriting correct code. It covers that line only
and is reported. Repeating it means the scope is wrong: narrow \`paths\`/\`exclude\`/\`absent\`.

- **test-gotcha-2026-01-01**: Do not use the old API

<!-- haive:sensors-end -->

<!-- haive:bridge-end -->
"
`;

